"A bound wand is bound to its wizard almost like an auriad, and grows fragile far from its owner."
"Giving one away is a profound gesture, a joyhurt; it returns when the recipient dies."
"Bound wands gain influence as they age, and pass to an heir by ritual."
"An owner feels a bound wand's destruction like losing an auriad; a destroyed wand fades from reality."
"A damaged owner connection can be remedied; swapping in the owner's other wand restrengthens it."
"A destroyed heirloom may be taken as an omen, or as an ancestral sin descendants must erase."
